        "id": 26167,
        "name": "Tegulus",
        "username": "Tegulus",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/46a35a/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-22T22:14:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Matchstickman&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Matchstickman\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So given that Ryan Frost* was essentially a normal guy before the accident and he rejected the offer of the suit the first time (and probably on many subsequent occasions) it was offered to him does anyone else feel that once he’s paid off his debt for the cyrosuit, 10 years of medical treatment and the cyro chamber that he’ll just go “I’m done, go find another guy to risk his life everyday”?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>With a name like that he should have known that some cold related accident was bound to happen to him.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah. But sometime later he would either witness a situation similar to one that killed his fiancee and he would be unable to help. Or some villain would be threatening one of his old teammates. You know, the one he had been developing feelings for? Then he would realize that his proper place is in his cryo-suit as a member of the Freedom Five.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:00:05.832Z",
